   "evidence": "naming-conventions.md: \"When referring to a namespaced definition in a lemma name not in the same namespace, the definition should have its namespace removed. If the definition name is unambiguous without its namespace, it can be used as is. Else, the namespace is prepended back to it in lowerCamelCase.\" Upstream `PowerSeries.rescale` exists (mathlib/Mathlib/RingTheory/PowerSeries/Substitution.lean:404 `rescale_eq_subst`), and the new `SubstGroup.rescale` is at Substitution.lean:183.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/QFT/Factorization/Evolution/BetaFunction.lean",
   "fix": "Rename to `transformBeta_substGroupRescale`, `pow_mul_betaCoeff_transformBeta_substGroupRescale`, `betaCoeff_transformBeta_substGroupRescale` (update the module docstring list at lines 64-65), or else rename `SubstGroup.rescale` to something not homonymous with `PowerSeries.rescale`.",
   "issue": "`transformBeta_rescale` (line 329), `pow_mul_betaCoeff_transformBeta_rescale` (337) and `betaCoeff_transformBeta_rescale` (346) use the bare token `rescale` for `EpsilonEridani.SubstGroup.rescale`, but the file does `open PowerSeries` (line 78) so bare `rescale` denotes `PowerSeries.rescale` \u2014 which appears on the RHS of line 330 (`C (u : R) * rescale (\u2191u\u207b\u00b9 : R) \u03b2`). The same token names two different functions in one statement; these lemmas are not in the `SubstGroup` namespace, so the naming convention requires the namespace back.",
   "line": "329"
  }
 ],
